That gives you cloud portability without cloud-dependent architecture.

And I would keep your frontend in Docker for now

So your production Compose can remain conceptually:

docker-compose.production.yml

nginx
frontend
backend
db

Don't remove the frontend just because you're thinking about disaster recovery.

The important thing is that the frontend is reproducible from your GitHub repository.

The irreplaceable things are:

        CODE → GitHub
        DATA → PostgreSQL backup
       FILES → Media backup
   CONFIG → secure environment backup

Everything else can be rebuilt.

My recommended FUTMxStore principle

Treat EC2 as cattle, not a pet.

If EC2 dies:

No panic.

You don't spend three days trying to resurrect the machine.

You provision another machine, restore:

CODE
+
DATABASE
+
MEDIA
+
CONFIG

and you're back online.

That is the architecture I would build around your 2–3 hour recovery requirement and near-zero budget.